{
  "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 8 (score 654.0, best so far): the oval finishes 18/20 and the s-bend 19/20, both improved by the narrower body (yaw inertia down). The slalom is still 0/20 finishes, with progress 0.47 (up from 0.23), max_error about 0.064 m and one line-loss event per run. The off-track limit stays at 0.06 m. Body_length (0.10) and body_width (0.08) are already at their minimums, so mass is the only remaining lever on yaw inertia (mass*(L^2+W^2)/12). Changing mass from 0.8 to 0.5 kg cuts inertia by about 37 percent, the largest remaining reduction, and should help the robot follow alternating slalom curves. Mass does not change the off-track limit. I keep the other controller values (kp 5.0, kd 1.2, ki 0, base_speed 1.1, last_direction) and the geometry (sensors at y 0.08, x -0.07 to 0.07, size 0.016, wheel_track 0.12) so the effect of mass alone can be read. Expected result: slalom progress above 0.6 and some finishes, s-bend finishes at or above 19/20, and oval steering_oscillation near 0.17 or below. Hypotheses: (H1) yaw inertia is still the main bend-lag term on the slalom, so lower mass raises its progress; (H2) if oval oscillation rises above 0.2, the faster yaw response is overshooting, and kd should go to about 1.5; (H3) if the slalom stays near 0.5 progress, the limit is sensor coverage or response speed on alternating curves, pointing to a 7-sensor array inside x = ±0.07 m or a higher kp with a lower base_speed. Measurements requested: per-track completion, progress, max_error, rms_error, line_loss_events and steering_oscillation, to separate lag from coverage loss.",
  "geometry": {
    "body_length": 0.1,
    "body_width": 0.08,
    "mass": 0.5,
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.07, "y": 0.08},
      {"x": -0.035, "y": 0.08},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.08},
      {"x": 0.035, "y": 0.08},
      {"x": 0.07, "y": 0.08}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "wheel_track": 0.12
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.1,
    "kp": 5.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 1.2,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort", "controller_errors", "noise_robustness"]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Lighter robot, mass 0.5",
      "notes": "Cuts mass from 0.8 to 0.5 kg, the last lever on yaw inertia after body_length and body_width hit their minimums. Iteration 8 showed that lower inertia raised slalom progress from 0.23 to 0.47, and this change tests whether it keeps going."
    }
  }
}
